WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.145 --> 00:00:02.228
(swoosh)

00:00:03.659 --> 00:00:06.416
- Step one is obsess, get totally focused,

00:00:06.416 --> 00:00:08.382
unleash your desire,
that gives the energy.

00:00:08.382 --> 00:00:10.089
Step two is not waiting.

00:00:10.089 --> 00:00:12.526
It's massive action, keep
changing your approach

00:00:12.526 --> 00:00:14.949
until you find effective execution.

00:00:14.949 --> 00:00:17.663
If you're running east
looking for a sunset,

00:00:17.663 --> 00:00:19.375
I don't care how positive you are,

00:00:19.375 --> 00:00:20.487
you're not going to see the sunset.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:21.320
It's the wrong strategy.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:22.205
- Not going to happen.

00:00:22.205 --> 00:00:23.076
- It's just not going to happen.

00:00:23.076 --> 00:00:25.054
So you got to have a proven strategy,

00:00:25.054 --> 00:00:26.206
and you can get there faster,

00:00:26.206 --> 00:00:27.714
same way I've done it with these books,

00:00:27.714 --> 00:00:28.997
just saying, "I could go this,

00:00:28.997 --> 00:00:30.899
"or I could spend four years,

00:00:30.899 --> 00:00:32.891
"interview 50 of the
smartest people in the world,

00:00:32.891 --> 00:00:34.398
"all billionaires that
started with nothing

00:00:34.398 --> 00:00:35.917
"and find out what they did,

00:00:35.917 --> 00:00:38.773
"and compress decades into days."

00:00:38.773 --> 00:00:41.169
That's really the purpose
of everything that I do.

00:00:41.169 --> 00:00:43.138
So when you have that plan

00:00:43.138 --> 00:00:44.395
and you keep changing your approach,

00:00:44.395 --> 00:00:45.847
I always tell people,

00:00:45.847 --> 00:00:47.305
"How long would you give your average kid

00:00:47.305 --> 00:00:48.779
"to learn how to walk

00:00:48.779 --> 00:00:50.426
"before you turned to the kid and said,

00:00:50.426 --> 00:00:51.541
"Dude, it's never going to happen.

00:00:51.541 --> 00:00:52.374
"You're not a walker.

00:00:52.374 --> 00:00:53.207
"Just give it up."

00:00:53.207 --> 00:00:54.040
People are like, "Are you crazy?

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.366
"My kid is going to keep trying until."

00:00:55.366 --> 00:00:56.511
Well that's really step two.

00:00:56.511 --> 00:00:58.015
You keep changing your
approach until you find it.

00:00:58.015 --> 00:01:00.025
And then the third step to achievement

00:01:00.025 --> 00:01:02.962
really is, simple as it may sound,

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:04.239
if you're obsessed,
you know what you want,

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:05.392
you're taking massive action,

00:01:05.392 --> 00:01:07.514
maybe you modeled somebody to
figure out the right action

00:01:07.514 --> 00:01:10.427
so you get there quicker,
and you're executing,

00:01:10.427 --> 00:01:12.283
you still need a little grace.

00:01:12.283 --> 00:01:15.727
Some people call it luck,
you could call it God,

00:01:15.727 --> 00:01:17.797
but I really believe that
there's the part we do

00:01:17.797 --> 00:01:19.482
and then there's the
part that comes to us,

00:01:19.482 --> 00:01:22.368
but I do know grace shows up a lot more

00:01:22.368 --> 00:01:24.385
when you do the first
two steps on your own,

00:01:24.385 --> 00:01:26.126
and grace shows up a lot more

00:01:26.126 --> 00:01:27.579
when you acknowledge grace in your life,

00:01:27.579 --> 00:01:29.701
when you acknowledge that
I was born in a world

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:31.207
where I didn't have to build this internet

00:01:31.207 --> 00:01:32.914
that I can pull out of my pocket

00:01:32.914 --> 00:01:34.043
the answer to everything on Earth.

00:01:34.043 --> 00:01:35.878
I'm driving on streets I didn't pave.

00:01:35.878 --> 00:01:38.116
I'm reading books I didn't have to write.

00:01:38.116 --> 00:01:39.341
That's the gift of our lives,

00:01:39.341 --> 00:01:41.275
and I think when we experience that grace,

00:01:41.275 --> 00:01:42.999
we don't just experience more achievement,

00:01:42.999 --> 00:01:44.850
but we start to experience
more fulfillment.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.978
- And grace not only effects
your ability to get there,

00:01:46.978 --> 00:01:49.543
but it effects what
you do and how you live

00:01:49.543 --> 00:01:50.673
once you are there.

00:01:50.673 --> 00:01:52.402
- It really determines
the quality of your life,

00:01:52.402 --> 00:01:56.243
because unless you live
in a state of gratitude...

00:01:56.243 --> 00:01:59.218
I did an interview with
Sir John Templeton,

00:01:59.218 --> 00:02:01.838
who as you know is one of the
first billionaire investors

00:02:01.838 --> 00:02:02.789
and just a brilliant man.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.176
He came from nothing,

00:02:04.176 --> 00:02:06.694
and he donated, I think it was 750,

00:02:06.694 --> 00:02:07.818
they still do it, The Templeton Fund,

00:02:07.818 --> 00:02:09.517
I think it's 750 million dollars a year,

00:02:09.517 --> 00:02:12.555
it's bigger than the Nobel
Fund that he donates,

00:02:12.555 --> 00:02:14.058
and one day I asked him, I said,

00:02:14.058 --> 00:02:16.340
"What is the secret to wealth?"

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:17.860
And he looked at me, paused,

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:19.921
this big smile and his
eyes got really bright

00:02:19.921 --> 00:02:22.175
like they always did, and he said,

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:23.699
"Tony, it's what you teach."

00:02:23.699 --> 00:02:25.928
And I said, "Well, I teach a
lot of things, which thing?"

00:02:25.928 --> 00:02:27.518
- He said, "Gratitude."

00:02:27.518 --> 00:02:29.226
He said, "Because you and I Tony

00:02:29.226 --> 00:02:31.737
"know billionaires that are miserable,

00:02:31.737 --> 00:02:33.460
"and it's because they're not
grateful for what they have.

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:36.224
"And we both know people
who have no money seemingly,

00:02:36.224 --> 00:02:37.890
"but they're so grateful for their health,

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.642
"for their husband, for their
wife, for their children,

00:02:39.642 --> 00:02:40.597
"they're so grateful to God,

00:02:40.597 --> 00:02:43.561
"they're so grateful for
their life that they're rich."

00:02:43.561 --> 00:02:46.280
So I think it starts with that gratitude.

00:02:46.280 --> 00:02:47.820
It starts with that connection to grace

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.015
as simplistic as that sounds.

00:02:49.015 --> 00:02:51.068
So it's not enough just to
have your financial plan.

00:02:51.068 --> 00:02:52.665
You can have all the
money and be miserable.

00:02:52.665 --> 00:02:54.918
Let's have the money and
be really rich emotionally,

00:02:54.918 --> 00:02:56.848
psychologically and spiritually.4

00:02:56.848 --> 00:02:58.931
(swoosh)

